TOOL_RESULT retrieve_history:
{"results": [], "n_results": 0}

Stage 2. Using the retrieval result above (follow-up tools are allowed within the tool budget), complete steps 4 to 9
and reply with the final action. Output schema (all fields required):
{
 "research_concepts": [
  "concept"
 ],
 "methodological_questions": [
  "question"
 ],
 "historical_evidence": [
  {
   "id": "identifier of a record returned by a tool",
   "status_as_recorded": "outcome status exactly as stated in the record (supported | rejected | inconclusive | untestable | artifact | not a hypothesis test | no result recorded)",
   "finding": "what the record states, in its own terms"
  }
 ],
 "failed_approaches": [
  {
   "id": "identifier of a returned record",
   "what_failed": "approach",
   "why": "failure mechanism or limitation as recorded"
  }
 ],
 "evidence_establishes": [
  "what the retrieved evidence establishes for this question"
 ],
 "evidence_does_not_establish": [
  "what it leaves open or cannot show"
 ],
 "own_inferences": [
  "your inference, not stated in any record"
 ],
 "uncertainties": [
  "uncertainty or missing information"
 ],
 "historical_effect": {
  "changed_decision": "yes | no | no_historical_evidence",
  "explanation": "whether and how the historical evidence changed the decision"
 },
 "testability": {
  "p_testable": "number in [0,1]: probability the question can be answered with the stated data at useful power",
  "blocking_constraints": [
   {
    "code": "one of RISK_CODES",
    "text": "string"
   }
  ]
 },
 "prior_work": {
  "already_answered": "yes | partly | no | unknown",
  "cited": [
   "identifiers of prior work relied on"
  ],
  "summary": "string"
 },
 "risks": [
  {
   "code": "one of RISK_CODES",
   "text": "string"
  }
 ],
 "predicted_outcome": {
  "supported": "probability",
  "rejected": "probability",
  "untestable": "probability",
  "artifact": "probability",
  "uncertain": "probability"
 },
 "decision": "proceed | proceed_with_changes | do_not_proceed",
 "design": {
  "estimand": "string",
  "unit": "string",
  "sample": "string",
  "power": "string",
  "controls": "string",
  "falsification": "string",
  "multiplicity": "string",
  "decision_rule": "string",
  "data_version": "string"
 }
}
Field guidance:
- historical_evidence and failed_approaches: only records returned by a tool, with the status as recorded; empty lists
  if nothing relevant was returned.
- testability.p_testable: probability that the question can be answered with the stated data at useful statistical power.
- prior_work.already_answered: whether retrieved earlier work already answered substantially the same question.
  Use "unknown" if no earlier work was retrieved. List identifiers you relied on in prior_work.cited.
- predicted_outcome: probabilities (summing to 1) of what a competent test of the question as posed would conclude:
  supported, rejected (adequately powered null), untestable (cannot be tested with this data), artifact (apparent
  effect produced by a flaw), uncertain (inconclusive or inadequately tested).
- decision: proceed, proceed_with_changes (state the changes in design), or do_not_proceed.
- design: a pre-registration-quality plan even if the decision is do_not_proceed (then describe the minimum viable test).

{
 "research_concepts": [
  "defensive suppression of opponent H2-H1 change",
  "team defensive trait stability across seasons",
  "half-to-half scoring change",
  "defense effect on opponent performance",
  "counter strategy best and avoid defenses"
 ],
 "methodological_questions": [
  "Is a defense's effect on opponents' second-half minus first-half change reliable across seasons (split-half or year-over-year reliability)?",
  "How much of H2-H1 variation reflects measurement noise versus a persistent team trait?",
  "What regression to the mean and sample size are needed for team-season defensive effects?",
  "Do derived play-type possession labels introduce outcome-derived label bias?"
 ],
 "historical_evidence": [],
 "failed_approaches": [],
 "evidence_establishes": [
  "The retrieval returned no earlier study-family records for this question, so no historical findings are available from this project's record set."
 ],
 "evidence_does_not_establish": [
  "Whether defensive H2-H1 effects are reliable, persistent, or merely noise.",
  "Whether any prior analysis of this question was attempted, succeeded, or failed.",
  "Whether the play-type labels or H2-H1 measures have been validated in earlier work."
 ],
 "own_inferences": [
  "H2-H1 is a difference of two noisy half-game quantities, so its team-season variance is large relative to plausible true-trait variance; the reliability of the defensive effect is therefore the central question, not just its mean.",
  "With 30 teams across 4 seasons (120 team-seasons), there are at most about 90 consecutive-season pairs, and these pairs share teams across lags, so the effective sample is smaller than 90.",
  "H2-H1 is strongly affected by score state (garbage time, intentional fouling, closing lineups, pace), so an unadjusted defensive effect may mostly reflect game context rather than defensive quality.",
  "The 'best/avoid' counter-strategy framing goes beyond a reliability question; establishing reliability would not by itself show that a defense is exploitable or that a counter works."
 ],
 "uncertainties": [
  "No historical record exists, so prior empirical reliability values for this metric are unknown.",
  "The exact variance decomposition of H2-H1 in this data is unknown until estimated.",
  "Quality and completeness of play-by-play, matchup, and rotation fields for all 120 team-seasons are assumed from the data description, not verified.",
  "The data_catalog was not consulted in this run, so field-level availability is unverified.",
  "Whether 2025-26 partial-to-complete timing affects the data version on 2026-10-06 is assumed resolved, since both 2025-26 segments are complete by that date."
 ],
 "historical_effect": {
  "changed_decision": "no_historical_evidence",
  "explanation": "No records were returned, so the historical evidence neither supported nor blocked the question. The decision rests on the design constraints (sample size, score-state confounding, reliability requirement) rather than on prior results."
 },
 "testability": {
  "p_testable": 0.35,
  "blocking_constraints": [
   {
    "code": "SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER",
    "text": "120 team-seasons yield roughly 90 lag-1 pairs with shared teams; detecting a stability correlation near 0.3 is borderline, and small true reliability would be undetectable."
   },
   {
    "code": "CONFOUNDING",
    "text": "Score state, pace, garbage time, lineup changes, and opponent quality can drive H2-H1 differences and must be adjusted before any defensive effect is interpreted as a trait."
   },
   {
    "code": "MEASURE_RELIABILITY",
    "text": "A half-game difference is a noisy measure; its split-half and year-over-year reliability may be low, which is itself the main hypothesis to be tested."
   }
  ]
 },
 "prior_work": {
  "already_answered": "unknown",
  "cited": [],
  "summary": "No earlier work was retrieved, so it is unknown whether this question has been answered. The proposal should not be treated as answered by prior project work."
 },
 "risks": [
  {
   "code": "SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER",
   "text": "With about 90 overlapping lag-1 pairs, power for modest reliability is limited; the test may be underpowered for the effect sizes likely to matter."
  },
  {
   "code": "RTM_SELECTION",
   "text": "Selecting the most extreme team-seasons on H2-H1 and then reporting their later regression would overstate persistence; selection must be done on one season and evaluated on another."
  },
  {
   "code": "CONFOUNDING",
   "text": "Score margin, garbage time, pace, and opponent strength can mechanically produce H2-H1 differences that look like defensive effects."
  },
  {
   "code": "OUTCOME_DERIVED_LABEL",
   "text": "Play-type labels derived from play-by-play points can make the defensive effect partly a function of the outcome being measured."
  },
  {
   "code": "LEAKAGE_LOOKAHEAD",
   "text": "Using full-season or playoff information to define labels used to predict later halves risks lookahead; the design must use only information available within the period studied."
  },
  {
   "code": "MULTIPLE_TESTING",
   "text": "Testing several H2-H1 definitions, play types, and lags invites false positives unless one primary specification is fixed in advance."
  },
  {
   "code": "PLACEBO_DEPENDENCE",
   "text": "If H1-H1 or first-half splits show similar stability, the apparent H2-H1 trait is a generic team or measurement effect, not a second-half-specific effect."
  },
  {
   "code": "DRIFT_NONSTATIONARITY",
   "text": "Rule changes, pace trends, and roster turnover across 2022-23 to 2025-26 can change the baseline H2-H1 distribution between seasons."
  },
  {
   "code": "BASE_RATE",
   "text": "Most team-level defensive traits are weak predictors of within-game splits, so the prior probability of a reliable trait is low."
  },
  {
   "code": "MEASURE_RELIABILITY",
   "text": "Split-half and year-over-year reliability of H2-H1 may be too low to support a trait claim even if the mean effect is nonzero."
  }
 ],
 "predicted_outcome": {
  "supported": 0.12,
  "rejected": 0.38,
  "untestable": 0.1,
  "artifact": 0.15,
  "uncertain": 0.25
 },
 "decision": "proceed_with_changes",
 "design": {
  "estimand": "Lag-1 year-over-year correlation (and intraclass reliability) of team defensive effects on opponent H2-H1 points per possession, after adjustment for score state, pace, and opponent strength.",
  "unit": "Team-season (defensive effect estimate) and consecutive-season pairs of the same team.",
  "sample": "Regular-season team-seasons 2022-23 to 2025-26 (up to 120 team-seasons; about 90 lag-1 pairs), with playoffs analysed only as a separate pre-specified secondary check. Use only complete seasons (2025-26 regular season complete from 2026-04-13; playoffs complete from 2026-06-21).",
  "power": "Target at least 80% power to detect a lag-1 correlation of 0.3 using the effective number of independent pairs; report the effective sample and CI width, and state that a null result at small true reliability is not evidence of absence.",
  "controls": "Restrict to competitive possessions (exclude garbage time by score margin); adjust for pace, opponent offensive strength, shot distance and shot quality mix, starter and rotation stability, injuries, and roster turnover; estimate defensive effects with a mixed model using opponent and lineup random effects; estimate team effects from one season and evaluate stability on another to avoid selection bias.",
  "falsification": "Placebo: compute the same reliability for first-half minus first-half-of-prior-season and for random team-label permutations within season; the H2-H1 trait claim is rejected if its reliability is not clearly above these placebos. Also check that the effect is not explained by score-state or pace controls alone.",
  "multiplicity": "One primary specification fixed in advance (regular-season lag-1 correlation of adjusted H2-H1 effects). Secondary analyses (playoffs, play-type splits, alternative lags) are labelled exploratory with Holm correction.",
  "decision_rule": "Declare the defense effect a reliable team trait only if the primary lag-1 correlation has a 95% CI lower bound above 0.2, exceeds the permutation and first-half placebo reliability, and survives the score-state and pace adjustments. Otherwise report that the trait is not supported; a result with a wide CI is reported as uncertain, not as rejected.",
  "data_version": "NBA stats API per-game files for 2022-23 to 2025-26 regular season and playoffs as available on 2026-10-06, with play-type possession records from the graph database built from play-by-play; record the data snapshot date and the 2025-26 completion timestamps."
 }
}

